# Section 4, Element Types, Reflective Gratings: the NEW dialog for a flat reflective grating (Grating,
# element 1; order 1, ruling 1.897366596E-06, h1HOE 1,0,0).  Dave 2026-10-19: regenerate the NEW tutorials as
# plain dialogs.  The element answers are 3.2's except h1HOE: 3.2 typed 0,1,0, but
# examples/GratingExample.in (the Appendix A.2 deck the text builds) has 1,0,0 and traces (3096 rays, DAvgCumL
# 9.16228), so the tutorial follows the deck (Dave 2026-10-20, #13).  Differences from 3.2: the current dialog asks 'Enter glass
# type (FixedIndex): [FixedIndex]:' before the index and extinction (answered with its default); it echoes the
# element and asks 'Is this correct? [YES]:' (default); the menus list the current element and surface types;
# the element block adds nCoat and prints h1HOE/OrderHOE/RuleWidth before IndRef/Extinc.  3.2 printed only the
# element, so the source (the Appendix A.2 deck's: collimated from z=-6 at normal incidence, 600 nm, 1 unit
# wide; 15 points here) and a flat FocalPlane at z=-3 are setup (not printed).  Pins: the element as SHOW
# prints it, and the mean path to the focal plane, 6 + 3/cos(asin(0.6/1.897366596)) = 6 + sqrt(10) = 9.16228,
# the first-order diffraction angle.
cd $TMP
new
grating
0,0,1
0,0,-6
1d22
1
0
none
6d-7
1
Circular
1
15
1,0,0
0,1,0
2
